    <%# EJS DOCUMENTATION: https://ejs.co/ %>
    COMMENT: ====================================================================================
    COMMENT: CUSTOM METHODS FOR SaveSlot OBJECT
    COMMENT: ====================================================================================
    
    COMMENT: Checks if this save slot contains any data.
    METHOD hasData(): Boolean
        
        PURPOSE: Determines if this save slot has been used to store data
        
        RETURNS: True if data exists, false if slot is empty
        
        WHY: Before loading data, you may want to check if the slot has data
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: url describes the CLOUD copy, and a local-only slot has none because
            COMMENT: there is nothing to fetch. Checking url alone would report a save made
            COMMENT: while offline as an empty slot, so when this slot is describing the
            COMMENT: local copy, its recorded size is what says whether data is there.
            IF this.source is "local" THEN
                RETURN this.size > 0
            END IF
            RETURN this.url is not null
    END METHOD
    
    COMMENT: Clears all data from this save slot.
    METHOD clearData(callback: Function, thisArg: Object)
        
        PURPOSE: Deletes the data stored in this save slot
        
        PARAMETERS:
            callback: Function to call when clearing is complete
            thisArg: Context to use when calling the callback
        
        WHY: Users may want to delete their save data or start over

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Refuse this outright on a slot loaded from another app. Slot ids
            COMMENT: are per-app SLOT NUMBERS, so an unguarded call here erases THIS
            COMMENT: app's slot of the same number - it succeeds, and the player loses
            COMMENT: their save. See BaseObject.assertNotForeign.
            CALL this.assertNotForeign("clearData()", "Slot numbers are per-app, so this would erase THIS app's slot " + this.id + " instead.")

            COMMENT: Dual-clear, local first. A cleared local copy with an unreachable
            COMMENT: cloud still counts as cleared - see saveDataRaw for the full rule.
            CREATE localOk AS false
            IF this.core is not null AND this.core.appState is not null THEN
                SET localOk TO this.core.appState.clearLocalSlotData(this.id)
            END IF

            COMMENT: Call CloudSave.clearSlot via the core wrapper
            IF this.core is not null THEN
                CALL this.core.callComponent("CloudSave.clearSlot", { id: this.id }, this.onWriteComplete, this, { callback: callback, thisArg: thisArg, localOk: localOk })
            ELSE
                COMMENT: Nothing to send, so the local leg decides the outcome on its own.
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                    PASSING null, (localOk ? null : NewgroundsIO.Errors.getError(0, "No core, and the local clear failed."))
            END IF
    END METHOD

    COMMENT: Loads the raw string data from the URL stored on this save slot.
    METHOD loadDataRaw(callback: Function, thisArg: Object)

        DO NOT ADD A FOREIGN-OBJECT GUARD HERE. This reads the absolute URL the server
        returned with the slot, so it needs no app context and works on another app's
        data unchanged - which is the entire point of being able to load another app's
        slots. Guarding it would break the read half of cross-app access. Only the
        WRITE methods on this class take assertNotForeign.

        PURPOSE: Retrieves unprocessed data from the cloud storage URL linked to this save slot
        
        PARAMETERS:
            callback: (required) Function to call with the raw data string (or null if load fails)
            thisArg: Context to use when calling the callback
        
        WHY: Some apps store large save files on external cloud URLs instead of inline
        
        IMPORTANT NOTE: The Newgrounds API v3 may not include the protocol (https://) in the URL.
        If the URL is missing the protocol, prepend "https:" to prevent load errors.
        Prepare for both cases - some URLs may already have the protocol.
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Consult `source`, do NOT work freshness out again here. It is the record
            COMMENT: of which copy won the merge, and the same property a game reads to draw
            COMMENT: its cloud badge, so the row's badge and the copy this returns cannot
            COMMENT: disagree. Recomputing freshness independently is how they drift apart.
            IF this.source is "local" AND this.core is not null AND this.core.appState is not null THEN
                CREATE localData AS this.core.appState.readLocalSlotData(this.id)
                IF localData is not null THEN
                    SET this.error TO null
                    CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                        PASSING localData
                    RETURN
                END IF
            END IF

            COMMENT: Check if URL exists and is not empty
            IF this.url is null OR this.url is empty THEN
                COMMENT: No URL stored - call callback with null
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                    PASSING null
                RETURN
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Prepare the URL for loading
            SET loadUrl TO this.url
            
            COMMENT: Add protocol if missing (URL may be missing "https:" prefix)
            IF loadUrl does not contain "://" THEN
                SET loadUrl TO "https:" + loadUrl
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Track the HTTP status separately from the outcome handlers, exactly as
            COMMENT: Core.sendRequest does - see Core.pseudo's onHTTPResponse for the full
            COMMENT: rationale. Start at UNKNOWN_STATUS and only overwrite it if your
            COMMENT: platform's URL loader genuinely reports one; never invent a status
            COMMENT: (a bare 500) for a load that may never have left the machine.
            CREATE httpStatus AS UNKNOWN_STATUS

            COMMENT: Load the data from the URL (implementation-specific)
            COMMENT: See IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE.txt for platform-specific URL loading patterns.
            COMMENT: If your loader exposes the status on a separate event/callback that
            COMMENT: fires before completion or failure, capture it into httpStatus there.
            TRY
                CALL LOAD_URL_ASYNC(loadUrl, FUNCTION onLoadComplete(data: String)
                    COMMENT: Load succeeded - clear any previous error
                    SET this.error TO null

                    COMMENT: Write-through cache, so this save is still readable next time the
                    COMMENT: cloud is not. Stamp it with THIS SLOT'S datetime, never the current
                    COMMENT: time: stamping it now would make the cached copy look newer than the
                    COMMENT: cloud copy it was just taken from, and the next merge would flip the
                    COMMENT: slot to local for no reason at all.
                    IF this.core is not null AND this.core.appState is not null THEN
                        CALL this.core.appState.writeLocalSlotData(this.id, data, this.datetime)
                    END IF

                    CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                        PASSING data
                END FUNCTION, FUNCTION onLoadError(error)
                    COMMENT: Load failed. Reuse Core's status-to-error mapping instead of a
                    COMMENT: hardcoded INVALID_RESPONSE, so a 404, a 503, a rate limit and a
                    COMMENT: dead connection are told apart rather than reported identically.
                    COMMENT: The cloud was the fresher copy, but the fetch itself failed (the
                    COMMENT: network dropped between listing and loading). Degrade to whatever
                    COMMENT: local copy exists rather than failing the whole load.
                    IF this.core is not null AND this.core.appState is not null THEN
                        CREATE cachedData AS this.core.appState.readLocalSlotData(this.id)
                        IF cachedData is not null THEN
                            SET this.error TO null
                            CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                                PASSING cachedData
                            RETURN
                        END IF
                    END IF

                    SET this.error TO NewgroundsIO.Errors.getError(
                        Core.errorCodeForHttpStatus(httpStatus),
                        Core.describeHttpStatus(httpStatus) + " (" + error.message + ")"
                    )
                    LOG_ERROR(this.error.message)
                    CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                        PASSING null
                END FUNCTION)
            CATCH loadError
                COMMENT: URL loading setup failed before any request went out - no status
                COMMENT: was ever possible, so this is always UNKNOWN_STATUS.
                SET this.error TO NewgroundsIO.Errors.getError(
                    Core.errorCodeForHttpStatus(UNKNOWN_STATUS),
                    Core.describeHttpStatus(UNKNOWN_STATUS) + " (" + loadError.message + ")"
                )
                LOG_ERROR(this.error.message)
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                    PASSING null
            END TRY
    END METHOD
    
    COMMENT: Loads data from the URL stored on this save slot and parses it as JSON.
    METHOD loadData(callback: Function, thisArg: Object)
        
        PURPOSE: Retrieves and decodes JSON data from the cloud storage URL linked to this save slot
        
        PARAMETERS:
            callback: (required) Function to call with the decoded object (or null if load/parse fails)
            thisArg: Context to use when calling the callback
        
        WHY: Combines URL loading and JSON parsing for external cloud-stored data
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Load the raw data from URL first
            CALL this.loadDataRaw WITH callback function
                SET decoded TO null
                
                COMMENT: If data was loaded successfully, decode it from JSON
                IF data is not null THEN
                    TRY
                        SET decoded TO JSON_DECODE(data)
                        COMMENT: JSON parsing succeeded - clear any previous error
                        SET this.error TO null
                    CATCH parseError
                        COMMENT: JSON parsing failed - set error property
                        SET this.error TO NewgroundsIO.Errors.getError(NewgroundsIO.Errors.INVALID_RESPONSE, "Failed to decode SaveSlot data JSON: " + parseError.message)
                        LOG_ERROR(this.error.message)
                        SET decoded TO null
                    END TRY
                ELSE
                    COMMENT: URL load failed (error already set by loadDataRaw)
                    COMMENT: decoded remains null
                END IF
                
                COMMENT: Return the decoded data to the user's callback
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                    PASSING decoded
            END callback function, WITH context this
    END METHOD
    
    COMMENT: Saves raw string data to this save slot.
    METHOD saveDataRaw(data: String, callback: Function, thisArg: Object)
        
        PURPOSE: Stores raw string data in this cloud save slot
        
        PARAMETERS:
            data: The raw string data to save
            callback: Function to call when saving is complete
            thisArg: Context to use when calling the callback
        
        WHY: Allows saving pre-formatted data without JSON encoding

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Same guard as clearData, and for the same reason - this is the
            COMMENT: call that would silently overwrite the player's own save.
            CALL this.assertNotForeign("saveDataRaw()", "Slot numbers are per-app, so this would overwrite THIS app's slot " + this.id + " instead.")

            COMMENT: Dual-write, local FIRST and then the cloud. A save that only reached
            COMMENT: local storage is still a save: telling the player it was lost when it is
            COMMENT: sitting on their machine is worse than reporting success and flagging it.
            COMMENT: It reaches the cloud on their next explicit save. Sync is PASSIVE - never
            COMMENT: auto-push a fresher local copy on its own.
            CREATE localOk AS false
            IF this.core is not null AND this.core.appState is not null THEN
                SET localOk TO this.core.appState.writeLocalSlotData(this.id, data)
            END IF

            COMMENT: Call CloudSave.setData via the core wrapper
            IF this.core is not null THEN
                CALL this.core.callComponent("CloudSave.setData", { id: this.id, data: data }, this.onWriteComplete, this, { callback: callback, thisArg: thisArg, localOk: localOk })
            ELSE
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                    PASSING null, (localOk ? null : NewgroundsIO.Errors.getError(0, "No core, and the local write failed."))
            END IF
    END METHOD

    COMMENT: Encodes data as JSON and saves it to this save slot.
    METHOD saveData(data: Object, callback: Function, thisArg: Object)
        
        PURPOSE: Encodes an object as JSON and saves it to the cloud
        
        PARAMETERS:
            data: The object to encode and save
            callback: Function to call when saving is complete
            thisArg: Context to use when calling the callback
        
        WHY: Simplifies saving - handles JSON encoding automatically

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Guarded here as well as in saveDataRaw, so the error names the
            COMMENT: method the caller actually used and a large object is not encoded
            COMMENT: before failing. The duplication is deliberate.
            CALL this.assertNotForeign("saveData()", "Slot numbers are per-app, so this would overwrite THIS app's slot " + this.id + " instead.")

            CREATE jsonString AS JSON_ENCODE(data)
            CALL this.saveDataRaw WITH jsonString, callback, thisArg
    END METHOD

    COMMENT: Returns a string representation of this save slot.
    METHOD toString(): String
        
        PURPOSE: Provides human-readable save slot representation
        
        RETURNS: SaveSlot description formatted as "SaveSlot #[id]"
        
        WHY: Allows convenient string conversion for logging, debugging, and display
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Return slot ID in readable format
            IF this.id is not null THEN
                RETURN "SaveSlot #" + this.id
            ELSE
                RETURN "SaveSlot #null"
            END IF
    END METHOD
    
    COMMENT: ====================================================================================
    COMMENT: Shared completion handler for saveDataRaw() and clearData().
    METHOD onWriteComplete(response: Response, callbackParams: Object)

        PURPOSE: Resolves the outcome of a cloud write and reports it to the developer

        PARAMETERS:
            response: The gateway response for CloudSave.setData or CloudSave.clearSlot
            callbackParams: Holds the developer's callback, their thisArg, and whether the local leg succeeded

        WHY: Both components return the same slot payload and follow the same partial-success
        rule, so both share one handler. localOk travels through callbackParams rather than
        living on the model, so two writes in flight cannot read each other's result.

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: A write can fail at either of two levels and BOTH have to be checked.
            COMMENT: The gateway returns HTTP success for a component that failed, so trusting
            COMMENT: the outer flag alone reports every rejected write as a success.
            CREATE error AS null
            IF response is null OR response.success is not true THEN
                COMMENT: Transport, or the request envelope itself.
                SET error TO response.error OR NewgroundsIO.Errors.getError(505)
            ELSE
                CREATE result AS response.getResult()
                IF result is null OR result.success is not true THEN
                    COMMENT: The request went through, but the component was rejected.
                    SET error TO result.error OR NewgroundsIO.Errors.getError(505)
                END IF
            END IF

            IF error is null THEN
                COMMENT: The cloud accepted it, so the cloud copy is canonical again.
                SET this.source TO "cloud"
            ELSE IF callbackParams.localOk is true THEN
                COMMENT: Partial success. The write exists locally and nowhere else, so report
                COMMENT: success and flag it, rather than telling the player a save they still
                COMMENT: have was lost. Fail only when NEITHER leg landed.
                SET this.source TO "local"
                SET error TO null
            END IF

            IF callbackParams.callback is not null THEN
                CALL callbackParams.callback WITH context callbackParams.thisArg
                    PASSING result, error
            END IF
    END METHOD

    COMMENT: SESSION MANAGEMENT METHOD
    COMMENT: ====================================================================================
    
    COMMENT: Clears session-specific data to return the save slot to its unauthenticated state.
    METHOD clearSessionData()
        
        PURPOSE: Resets user-specific save slot data while keeping the slot structure intact
        
        WHY: Called by AppState.onSessionCleared() when the user's session expires or is cleared
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            SET this.datetime TO null
            SET this.timestamp TO 0
            SET this.size TO 0
            SET this.url TO null

            COMMENT: Deliberately do NOT reset source. Everything above is cloud state,
            COMMENT: owned by the server and meaningless once the session ends. The local
            COMMENT: copy is not session-scoped: it survives sign-out, which is much of the
            COMMENT: point of having it. Resetting source to "cloud" would also claim this
            COMMENT: slot describes a cloud copy that was just wiped, which is the opposite
            COMMENT: of the truth when the local mirror is the only copy left.
    END METHOD
